Z||000000||Necromancer||09-21-2000||08:32 PM||||Well, I've searched back through the archives and can't find a definitive answer, so here goes.<P>I can get a 3.l aluminum head v6 from a '91 Beretta for the low low price of a ride home for it in my truck.<P>Now, how can I use this bad boy in my 85 GT? (very tired 2.8, 150k+ miles, nice oil smoker)<P>I can't get the Beretta ECM or harness, just the motor.<P>I was thinking any of the following:<P>1) Use the 3.1 block and crank, replace with the proper pistons for iron heads, and bring the heads and up over from the 2.8 after fixing 'em up<P>2) Try harder to find the thread about making the Fiero ECM run the DIS setup on the aluminum head motor. (I *know* I just saw something about that). Aside from the intake difference and the ECM, is the rest plug and play (exhaust, accessory mounts, etc)<P>3) ??????<P>Thanks!<P>-ken<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||09-21-2000||10:06 PM||||You didn't say if this was a known good running 3.1 engine or an unknown "probably needs rebuilt" engine. If it probably needs rebuilt, rob the crank, balancer, and flywheel (or flexplate) and rebuild your 2.8 into a 3.1 motor.<P>If you decide to use the 3.1, I think if you use pistons for the cast iron heads like you mentioned, and use the Fiero intake and accessories and most of the other goodies, that should work too.<P>Another option if the 3.1 is good is to find a wrecker 3.1 ECM and engine wiring from a car with the same tranny you plan on using. This is probably muchmore work than it sounds like. <p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
